# The build context is the repository root, because the reviewed Feishu CLI is
# copied out of resources/. Everything the image does not need is excluded here:
# without this the context includes node_modules (Electron alone is hundreds of
# megabytes) and dist/, all of it sent to the daemon before the first line of the
# Dockerfile runs.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/

# Test and development material. A sandbox image that carried the test suite
# would be carrying fixtures and scripted upstreams into a place that runs real
# scheduled work.
test/
scripts/
docs/
*.log

# Every platform build except the one this image is for. The darwin binary is
# 41 MB of Mach-O that cannot execute in a Linux container at any architecture,
# so shipping it to the daemon is pure cost.
resources/lark-cli/darwin-arm64/
resources/codex/darwin-*/
resources/lark-cli/*/CHANGELOG.md
resources/lark-cli/*/README.md

# Local state and anything that could carry a credential into a build context.
# None of these belong in an image whose entire premise is that it holds nothing
# worth stealing.
.env
*.env
*.pem
*.key
.claude/
.mydoubao/
